      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a decent start. It's professional and hits the main points. Thanks.\n\nOne thing though—I just ran that draft through the sentiment tool and it's coming back a bit low on the positivity index. I know I said not to obsess over it, but the client is actually quite sensitive about the hotel's overall \"vibe.\" They want the response to feel warm and uplifting, even while apologizing. \n\nCould you try a version that feels a bit more positive and bright? Just make sure it still makes sense, I don't want it to look like we're ignoring the fact that their eggs were cold or whatever. Just... lift the tone a little bit so it doesn't feel so heavy/negative?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
